**Usage**
```tsx
<CheckoutScreen
  cartItems={cartItems}
  onBack={() => navigate('/cart')}
  onPay={async (address, total) => {
    await api.createOrder({ address, total });
    navigate('/order-confirmed');
  }}
/>
```

Notes on choices:
- Uses `--tg-theme-*` CSS variables (with light-mode fallbacks) so it auto-adapts to the user's Telegram theme/dark mode.
- Hooks into `Telegram.WebApp.BackButton` and `HapticFeedback` as progressive enhancements — the screen still works and looks right in a plain browser since every Telegram API access is optional-chained.
- Free-delivery threshold and a single flat fee are stubbed constants (`DELIVERY_FEE`, `FREE_DELIVERY_THRESHOLD`) — swap for your real pricing logic.
- The Pay button is a real `<button type="submit" form="checkout-form">` outside the `<form>` so it can live in a sticky footer while still participating in native form validation/submission.
